lib/security.c contains the Mega CD security block, a region-specific
sequence of code and data created by Sega. The Mega CD Boot ROM refuses to
run any disc that does not carry this block unmodified at the start of its
Initial Program, so every bootable Mega CD disc, licensed or not, contains
it. Megadev reproduces it unmodified, as distributed with the Mega CD
development documentation, solely so that discs built with Megadev boot. It
is Sega's property and is not relicensed here.

The block includes the text "PRODUCED BY OR UNDER LICENCE FROM SEGA
ENTERPRISES LTD." and the Sega logo, which the Boot ROM displays when a disc
starts. That text and logo are part of Sega's block, not a statement by
Megadev or by any project built with it. Megadev and projects built with it
are not produced by or under license from Sega.

